OL,3,CProgramme listings for TUE 7 APR
OL,4,G1930FRadio 3 in Concert
OL,5,     GThe BBC National Orchestra and
OL,6,     GChorus of Wales are joined by
OL,7,     Gconductor Thomas Zehetmair to
OL,8,     Gperform Brahms's German Requiem
OL,9,     Gand Mozart's 40th Symphony.
OL,10,G2145FThe Essay: Healing Musicians
OL,11,     GKate Kennedy talks to prize-
OL,12,     Gwinning pianist Stephen Marquiss
OL,13,     Gabout the injury that nearly
OL,14,     Gdestroyed his career and what he
OL,15,     Gdid to establish a new
OL,16,     Grelationship with his instrument.
OL,17,G2200FNight Tracks
OL,18,     GSara Mohr-Pietsch presents an
OL,19,     Gadventurous, immersive soundtrack
OL,20,     Gfor late-night listening, from
OL,21,     Gclassical to contemporary and
OL,22,     Geverything in between.
